WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.558
Preflight checks confirm aircraft condition, propeller security, battery status, controller operation, navigation readiness, payload attachment, storage capacity, and required settings.

00:00:09.558 --> 00:00:16.894
The crew should also verify the area, weather, communications, and emergency plan immediately before launch.

00:00:16.894 --> 00:00:27.341
Maintain visual line of sight when required and operationally appropriate so the aircraft's position, orientation, flight path, and surrounding hazards remain understandable.

00:00:27.341 --> 00:00:35.566
A video feed narrows attention and may hide obstacles, people, or other aircraft outside the camera view.

00:00:35.566 --> 00:00:42.457
Situational awareness includes the aircraft, airspace, weather, crew, bystanders, vehicles, and changing ground conditions.

00:00:42.457 --> 00:00:49.348
Establish safe distances and prevent unbriefed people from entering the launch or recovery area.

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:54.016
Pause mission tasks when basic aircraft control needs attention.

00:00:54.016 --> 00:01:02.241
Loss of signal, unexpected navigation behavior, low battery, wind increase, and obstacle conflict require prompt conservative action.

00:01:02.241 --> 00:01:08.687
Follow the planned response and prioritize a safe landing over completing data collection.

00:01:08.687 --> 00:01:13.355
Automated behavior must be understood before it is needed.

00:01:13.355 --> 00:01:24.247
Flyaway risk can be reduced through maintenance, configuration checks, current situational awareness, and appropriate operating limits, but it cannot be reduced to zero.

00:01:24.247 --> 00:01:33.805
Know how to warn the crew, protect people, record the last known information, and report an event through required channels.

00:01:33.805 --> 00:01:37.584
Crew communication should be brief and unambiguous.

00:01:37.584 --> 00:01:42.697
Call important hazards, battery thresholds, signal changes, and landing status.

00:01:42.697 --> 00:01:48.254
Any crew member should be able to raise a safety concern.

00:01:48.254 --> 00:01:55.145
The pilot responsible for the flight must be willing to stop when margins disappear.
